;; weight on a compound FORMULA (not just a literal): each formula reifies to a
;; fresh determined atom (WEIGHTED-FORMULA n) via the count-neutral biconditional
;; A <=> phi, and the weight rides on that atom.  The trailing literal case still
;; emits a bare (WEIGHT <literal> w) line, unchanged.
(weight (and a b) 3.0)
(weight (or c d) 2.0)
(weight (not (and e f)) 1.5)
(weight (buy banana) 1.25)
